      "message": "Any particular reason why use `u32`, not `int`?\n\nIt looks like throughout KVM code it is used as `int`, not `u32` (in particular, in these `set_segment`, `get_segment`, `get_segment_base` kvm_x86_ops callbacks, as well as in our `pkvm_hc_data-\u003eset_segment` etc), so it\u0027s better to use `int` here as well, for consistency?\n\nAnd also it looks like it is mostly used as an array index etc, not for writing its value to VMCS hardware or whatever, so `int` seems more appropriate?",
