      "message": "\u003e Any particular reason why use u32, not int?\n\nFound that, we still need to make sure `seg \u003e 0` if it is int otherwise a negative seg can still cause out-of-bound access.\n\nTo simplify the check, change to `u32` rather than `int`.\n\nFor pKVM, these functions are dealing with the untrusted inputs from the host, seems `u32` is safer than `int`?",
